{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B2t-Wmr_zvm9g-PF8",
	"notes": "A Militarum Tempestus Scion: Schola Progenium-raised, hot-shot lasgun (\"hellgun\") armed, an elite special-operations trooper rather than a line Guardsman. Point math: ST 12 (+20), DX 14 (+80), IQ 11 (+20), HT 13 (+30) = 150; advantages +40; disadvantages -55; skills +71. Total 206 points, inside framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier, toward its lower end (a veteran Inquisitorial acolyte or Battle Sister should sit higher). No psychic abilities here; add from the separate psyker power library if a GM wants a Scion with sanctioned psyker support attached.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tJInSkJlHvRSxqkpE",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Schola Progenium physical conditioning is harder than ordinary Guard basic training.\n\nDesign: ST 12 (+2 from baseline), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t3QSqepfbRUdZ_Iow",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scions are drilled from childhood in the Schola Progenium specifically for weapons proficiency and small-unit special operations; Only War and Dark Heresy both model Tempestus Scions with noticeably better combat stats than a line Guardsman, used here for relative calibration.\n\nDesign: DX 14 (+4 from baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 80,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 4
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tDEhzf9X5KEJZaFdJ",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Schola Progenium education is broader and more rigorous than Guard basic training's rote drilling.\n\nDesign: IQ 11 (+1 from baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tKUE9Bcll-07IX6LV",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Selected and conditioned for endurance under Schola Progenium's harsher regimen.\n\nDesign: HT 13 (+3 from baseline), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 30,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 3
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t7vvdfZ6Ma9zp5Aqb",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Special-operations conditioning against freezing under fire.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tvhFnW9Rwjg6DQFjl",
			"name": "Very Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Schola Progenium physical training exceeds ordinary Guard fitness standards.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Very Fit (B55), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "t7C943CaWsZWkiAoW",
			"name": "High Pain Threshold",
			"reference": "B59",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Conditioning and selection produce troopers who keep fighting through wounds that would drop a conscript.\n\nDesign: Basic Set High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tHbTmFemmnbk1-gWm",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The God-Emperor)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Schola Progenium indoctrination is, if anything, more thorough than a regular Guard upbringing.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, taken for \"the Emperor/the Imperial Creed\" as the group/ideal. Not leveled in Basic Set.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tbXkOzom_8Njh8vhH",
			"name": "Duty (Astra Militarum)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Militarum Tempestus is an Astra Militarum special-operations arm; the same near-absolute service obligation applies.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133): almost-always-on-duty, hazardous, involuntary military service, at the top of the disadvantage's standard cost range.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tlVRMuTIBiLGp36AA",
			"name": "Sense of Duty (Squadmates)",
			"reference": "B153",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scion kill-teams are small and tight-knit; Schola Progenium \"siblings\" bonds are a recurring Black Library and Only War beat.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Sense of Duty (B153), small-group scope, -5.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tAuozKt6nRpzphant",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "ty2Wy4eSkOYIpKWeg",
			"name": "Intolerance (Heretics)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Schola-raised Scions are frequently used against internal Imperial threats (rogue PDF, cultists), and are indoctrinated accordingly.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), narrow-category cost (-5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tQ9yz3mcPzfClWU-N",
			"name": "Overconfidence",
			"reference": "B148",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scions are the Guard's acknowledged elite and are written (Only War's Tempestus material, and their portrayal as an intervention force called in when line infantry fails) as knowing it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Overconfidence (B148), -5.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		}
	],
